    <!-- When to Use Section -->
    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;">
      <h2>When to Use Strong Passwords vs. Passphrases</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Random Character Passwords (16+ chars):</strong> Best for password managers (e.g. 1Password, Bitwarden, Apple Keychain) where credentials are auto-filled and never memorized.</li>
        <li><strong>Memorable Passphrases (4-6 words):</strong> Best for master passwords, laptop login screens, Wi-Fi router keys, and mobile unlock PINs that humans need to type regularly.</li>
        <li><strong>Batch Generation (3–10 passwords):</strong> Quickly provision initial accounts for teams or generate secure tokens for staging API environments.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
